// TabcToggleBtn -> TcxButton  (ORM3 CLIENT, first authored 2026-09-14)
//
// STARTER DRAFT, written from the CORPUS rather than from guesswork. Measured on
// CLIENT\VARINSP.DFM: 20 TabcToggleBtn instances, every one of them setting
// Picture.Data / NumGlyphs / Style / GroupIndex / Caption, and 18 of them setting
// Images and Layout.
//
// >>> TWO THINGS HERE DO NOT VALIDATE YET, AND THAT IS AN ENGINE BUG, NOT A TYPO.
//
// Every OptionsImage.* path below is real -- `surface --qname
// cxButtons.TcxButtonImageOptions` lists Glyph, Images, Layout, Margin, NumGlyphs,
// Spacing -- but `proptree` does not expand OptionsImage, so the editor cannot
// offer or validate those paths today. See
// docs\INBOX-forward-decl-shadows-real-class-declaration.md.
//
// Until that lands, the lines marked PENDING will be reported as unknown paths.
// They are written out anyway so the rule is ready the day it clears, and so the
// engine team has a concrete acceptance case.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Layout needs a MAPPING, not an enum cast: one source value has to set TWO
// target properties.
//
// TabcButtonLayout has 6 members, TButtonLayout has 4. Four map straight across.
// ablGlyphCenter has no single equivalent -- in the VCL the glyph and caption are
// centred TOGETHER by setting Margin = -1 (Vcl.Buttons.pas:1285-1304: with
// Margin = -1 the layout code computes Margin := (ClientSize - TotalSize + 1) div 2
// over glyph+Spacing+text, i.e. it centres the PAIR instead of pinning the glyph
// to an edge). TcxButtonImageOptions.Margin is already `default -1`.
//
// ablGlyphTiled is DELIBERATELY UNMAPPED and there is no #else: it has no honest
// target, and an unmapped value is reported rather than guessed. No instance in
// VARINSP uses it.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#mapping AbcGlyphLayout from Abcbtn.TabcButtonLayout to cxButtons.TcxButton
#mapping AbcGlyphLayout #when Layout = ablGlyphLeft   -> OptionsImage.Layout = blGlyphLeft
#mapping AbcGlyphLayout #when Layout = ablGlyphRight  -> OptionsImage.Layout = blGlyphRight
#mapping AbcGlyphLayout #when Layout = ablGlyphTop    -> OptionsImage.Layout = blGlyphTop
#mapping AbcGlyphLayout #when Layout = ablGlyphBottom -> OptionsImage.Layout = blGlyphBottom
#mapping AbcGlyphLayout #when Layout = ablGlyphCenter -> OptionsImage.Layout = blGlyphLeft, OptionsImage.Margin = -1

#convert Abcbtn.TabcToggleBtn -> cxButtons.TcxButton, cxButtons, dxCore

#apply AbcGlyphLayout

// --- the image surface: what the owner asked for ---------------------------
// PENDING (see header): OptionsImage does not expand in proptree yet.
// Picture is TPicture, Glyph is TdxSmartGlyph -- bridged by the shipped
// `cast AssignGraphic` in casts.castlib, whose pas template is
// '{dst}.Assign({src});'. convert-apply does not yet REALISE that template; see
// docs\INBOX-2026-09-14-converter-to-engine-realize-class-casts.md.
#link OptionsImage.Glyph <- Picture : AssignGraphic
#link OptionsImage.Images <- Images
#link OptionsImage.NumGlyphs <- NumGlyphs

// --- direct, same-named, no cast needed ------------------------------------
// These validate today. Auto-Match finds the rest: the two property trees share
// 105 identical leaf paths (measured), so most of this file should be generated
// rather than typed.
#link Caption <- Caption
#link Down <- Down
#link GroupIndex <- GroupIndex
#link AllowAllUp <- AllowAllUp
#link Enabled <- Enabled
#link Visible <- Visible
#link Anchors <- Anchors
#link Align <- Align
#link Hint <- Hint
#link ShowHint <- ShowHint

// NOT carried: TabOrder / TabStop. Drafted here by habit and REJECTED by
// convert-validate -- TabcToggleBtn is a graphic control with no window handle,
// so it has neither. TcxButton does, and will get the VCL defaults. If tab order
// matters on the converted form it has to be set by hand, because there is no
// source value to carry.

// --- NOT carried, on purpose ------------------------------------------------
// Style = absThinHighlight is an Orpheus/abc paint style with no TcxButton
// equivalent; TcxButton's look comes from the active skin. Left for the operator
// rather than mapped to something that merely compiles.
